## Context

Audit 0127 drifts B, C, C2: PEP section 12 was written before the
`Tags:` -> `Tag:` rename shipped. Multiple issues:

1. Heading reads "Tags header" — should be "Tag header" (drift B).
2. Body says `A Tags: header was added`, `Tags is repeatable`, and
   argues against the rename (`Renaming to Tag: (singular) would
   weaken this`) — the rename already shipped (drift C).
3. Enum values list `post-talk, post-conference` alongside
   `needs-human, deferred` — code defaults reject the first two
   without .ergrc override (drift C2).

## Actions

- Rename heading to "Tag header: a closed enum for workflow labels".
- Rewrite prose to use `Tag:` (singular) throughout.
- Remove or update the anti-rename argument — it is now historical.
- Update enum list to match code defaults (`needs-human, deferred`),
  noting that `.ergrc [tags]` can extend the vocabulary.
- Mark PEP section as "GENERATED by Claude" per author convention.

## Exit criteria

- PEP section 12 uses `Tag:` singular consistently.
- No argument against the rename remains.
- Enum values match code defaults.
- `make test` passes (no code changes).
